{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureBindingFormArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureBindingFormArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasureFromFrobeniusPairing","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BranchingPushforwardMultiplicativity"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.bindingForm_tensor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.BranchingData.bindingForm_tensor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureBindingFormArchimedean.lean#L47-L58","doc":"**The binding form is a function of the `y`-weighted entangled deviation alone.**\nAgainst the free product of two marginals with non-vanishing traces,\n`B = −α · log(1 + Σ_λ y_λ δ_λ / (tr_M(a) tr_M(b)))`. Nothing else about the composite\nenters: two composites with the same weighted deviation bind identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.bindingForm_eq_zero_of_entangledSupp_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.bindingForm_eq_zero_of_entangledSupp_empty","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureBindingFormArchimedean.lean#L28-L36","doc":"**No shared block, no binding.** If the bound word and its free constituent\nproduct agree on every block character, the logarithmic binding vanishes. The\ncontrapositive: a nonzero binding forces a block on which the two characters\ndiffer — the \"entangled\" block set is non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.bindingForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockMeasure.FrobeniusPairingData.bindingForm","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockMeasureBindingFormArchimedean.lean#L23-L26","doc":"The logarithmic binding form `B = −α · log(tr_M(atom) / tr_M(free))` used by the\ncorpus's log-assembly binding routes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}